{%- comment -%}
  A cart line's price, with what it was struck through and what it saves.

  The "was" price comes from whichever source applies to the line, because
  Shopify reports no discount on a subscription: a selling plan sets the line's
  own price, so original_line_price equals final_line_price and total_discount
  is zero. The plan's allocation carries compare_at_price instead.

  In order: the plan's compare-at for a subscription line, the variant's
  compare-at for a one-time line, and original_line_price if a cart discount
  has beaten both. Nothing renders but the price when there is no saving to
  show, so a full-price line stays quiet rather than reading "Save $0".

  Accepts: item (a cart line item).
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- assign was_unit = 0 -%}
{%- if item.selling_plan_allocation and item.selling_plan_allocation.compare_at_price > item.final_price -%}
  {%- assign was_unit = item.selling_plan_allocation.compare_at_price -%}
{%- elsif item.variant.compare_at_price > item.final_price -%}
  {%- assign was_unit = item.variant.compare_at_price -%}
{%- endif -%}

{%- assign was_line = was_unit | times: item.quantity -%}
{%- if item.original_line_price > was_line -%}
  {%- assign was_line = item.original_line_price -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- assign saved = was_line | minus: item.final_line_price -%}

{%- if saved > 0 -%}
  <s class="cart-line-was">{{ was_line | money_without_trailing_zeros }}</s>
  <span class="cart-line-now">{{ item.final_line_price | money_without_trailing_zeros }}</span>
  <span class="cart-line-save">(Save {{ saved | money_without_trailing_zeros }})</span>
{%- else -%}
  <span class="cart-line-now">{{ item.final_line_price | money_without_trailing_zeros }}</span>
{%- endif -%}
